# Agents — how to navigate this knowledge base

This file mirrors `CLAUDE.md` for agent runtimes that prefer `AGENTS.md`. Both contain the same rules; whichever your agent reads first wins.

See [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) for the full ruleset.

## Quick reference

```
INDEX.md              ←  start here, every session
docs/<slug>/TOC.md    ←  outline of one document
docs/<slug>/document.md ←  full Markdown, read SLICES only
docs/<slug>/assets/   ←  raw images (don't read; description below them)
docs/<slug>/descriptions.json  ←  cached structured image descriptions

./scripts/search.sh "term" [slug]
./scripts/search_sections.sh "term"
./scripts/doclens.sh report     # coverage of image descriptions
```

## One-liner workflow

> User asks a factual question grounded in the source PDFs?
> → `Read INDEX.md` → identify slug(s) → `Read docs/<slug>/TOC.md` → grep with line offset → `Read document.md offset=<L> limit=200`.
